WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.436 --> 00:00:04.392
Unit eighteen. Coding with Sprites!

2
00:00:05.315 --> 00:00:09.719
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emily, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:09.769 --> 00:00:12.387
Hi, Ms. Emily! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:12.437 --> 00:00:16.151
Today we learn about Coding with Sprites. Let's go!

5
00:00:17.841 --> 00:00:21.707
Sprite. Say it with me. Sprite!

6
00:00:25.268 --> 00:00:29.493
Character. Say it with me. Character!

7
00:00:33.004 --> 00:00:37.471
Block coding. Say it with me. Block coding!

8
00:00:40.909 --> 00:00:45.109
Move block. Say it with me. Move block!

9
00:00:48.601 --> 00:00:52.420
Costume. Say it with me. Costume!

10
00:00:55.934 --> 00:00:59.892
Stage. Say it with me. Stage!

11
00:01:03.437 --> 00:01:07.437
Animate. Say it with me. Animate!

12
00:01:10.875 --> 00:01:14.625
Program. Say it with me. Program!

13
00:01:18.173 --> 00:01:27.167
In block coding, a sprite is a character I can program to move. I choose a costume and use a move block to animate it on the stage.

14
00:01:27.217 --> 00:01:30.857
Now I understand. Thank you, Ms. Emily!

15
00:01:31.899 --> 00:01:37.117
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:38.505
Block coding!

17
00:01:39.689 --> 00:01:45.064
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:45.114 --> 00:01:46.264
Animate!

19
00:01:47.212 --> 00:01:55.065
Did you know? The term 'sprite' in computer graphics dates back to some of the earliest video games ever made!

20
00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:57.492
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:58.385 --> 00:02:07.401
Think and answer. What kind of sprite character would you like to program?

22
00:02:07.451 --> 00:02:08.601
Great answer!

23
00:02:09.684 --> 00:02:15.227
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:15.277 --> 00:02:18.943
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

